@segment 6-9 Goldshire, Fargodeep Mine & Crystal Lake
@start-level 6
@carry 54,2158,91772,96627
@done 21,91752,91758
# Human Warlock 6-9, from the Human Mage route's segment 02 (same quests, same order). Changed for the warlock:
# the trainer is Maximillian Crowe in the basement of the Lion's Pride Inn (Elwynn Forest 44.4, 66.2), combat
# hints are written for a warlock with the Imp, food and drink are bought or looted.
# Sam's camp -> Goldshire (bind, train) -> the farms south of Goldshire (Maclure Vineyards,
# Stonefield Farm, Fargodeep Mine between them) -> Goldshire -> Crystal Lake (the fishermen and their murlocs)
# -> the fields south of Goldshire and Maybell -> Goldshire.
# Quest order of the farm loop follows TUGs' Elwynn file (in our own words). Differences from TUGs:
#  - No deliberate deaths: TUGs dies on purpose to get back to Goldshire. You walk or hearth.
#  - The fishermen's whole chain is in (TUGs only does the first two): 99127 A Net Disaster, 99143 Bottles and
#    Baubles, then 99128 Slimy Menace -> 99129 A Man About a Murloc -> 99130 An Enticing Offer -> 99131 Baited
#    for Success. The order inside that chain is NOT published: the steps assume each quest opens when the one
#    before is handed in. If Jason offers something else, take what he offers and tick or skip to match.
#  - The Escape (114, Maybell) is in: its walk south is shared with the duskweed fields of 99130.
# Book Return 91775 is flagged ELITE on its page (the back of the Fargodeep Mine). TUGs does it solo; the step
# says how, and how to leave it.
# Left out: 88 Princess Must Die! (a level 9 boar with two guards: not soloable for a warlock of 8), 91777 Rare
# Books (elite, back of the Jasperlode Mine, hand-in far away in Northshire), 91751 Rough Wolf Pelts and 97924
# (need Skinning), 91753 An Enchanting Lesson (needs Enchanting), 16 Give Gerard a Drink (no XP), 95771 A Taste
# of Darkness (no giver published).
# Unverified: that Homer Stonefield sells Shiny Red Apples in Forever (he does in the Questie data); they are
# for the Applejack Still in segment 04.
# Hearthstone: bound in Goldshire at the start, used once (back from the Fargodeep Mine).
# Carry-out: 61 Shipment to Stormwind (segment 04), 76 The Jasperlode Mine, 35 Further Concerns (segment 03).

# --- Sam's camp, on the way in ---
T 96627 | Sam Sarsaparilla sits at a campfire beside the road, just north-east of Goldshire
A 95998 | Sam Sarsaparilla
C 95998 @ Elwynn Forest, 45.0, 63.3 | Type /sit next to Sam's Basic Campfire and stay seated until you get the Boosted Rest buff
T 95998 | Sam Sarsaparilla
A 96626 | Sam Sarsaparilla: he sends you to the cook in Goldshire

# --- Goldshire ---
T 91772 | Marshal Dughan, in front of the smithy in Goldshire
A 91775 @ Elwynn Forest, 42.1, 65.9 | Marshal Dughan: Book Return. He gives you a book bag
T 54 | Marshal Dughan
A 62 | Marshal Dughan
A 47 | Remy "Two Times", a few steps south of Dughan
T 2158 | Innkeeper Farley, in the Lion's Pride Inn
S Goldshire | Make the Lion's Pride Inn your home
A 60 | William Pestle, in the inn
C 96626 @ Elwynn Forest, 44.4, 66.0 | Tomas, the cook in the inn's kitchen: learn Cooking from him (a few copper)
T 96626 | Tomas. You can now set up a basic camp fire of your own
N Learn First Aid from Michelle Belle in the inn @ Elwynn Forest, 43.4, 65.5 | A warlock has no heal at this level: bandages are your only one. Keep every Linen Cloth and turn it into Linen Bandages from now on
TRAIN @ Elwynn Forest, 44.4, 66.2 | Maximillian Crowe, the warlock trainer, in the basement of the inn (the stairs down are at the back): level 6 spells (Life Tap, Shadow Bolt rank 2). Life Tap turns health into mana: use it when your health is higher than your mana, then eat. Buy food and drink from the innkeeper

# --- The farms and the Fargodeep Mine ---
A 106 | Take the road south out of Goldshire to the Maclure Vineyards. Maybell Maclure is in the barn at the south end
N Kill Stonetusk Boars on the walk west to the Stonefield Farm until you have 4 Chunks of Boar Meat @ Elwynn Forest, 37.7, 82.5 | They are for the pie quest you get in a minute. The boars (5-6) graze on the slopes between the two farms, in front of the mine
A 85 | "Auntie" Bernice Stonefield, in front of the farmhouse at the Stonefield Farm
N Buy 4 Shiny Red Apples from Homer Stonefield @ Elwynn Forest, 33.7, 82.9 | He sells fruit at the farm. Do NOT eat them: the Applejack Still north of Westbrook Garrison turns them into a quest item in segment 04. If he does not sell them, tick this: kobolds and Defias drop them too
T 106 | Tommy Joe Stonefield stands by the river, west of the farm
A 111 | Tommy Joe Stonefield
T 111 | Gramma Stonefield, in the farmhouse
A 107 | Gramma Stonefield. The note goes to William Pestle in Goldshire
T 85 | Back east to the Maclure Vineyards: Billy Maclure, in front of the house
A 86 | Billy Maclure
C 86 @ Elwynn Forest, 37.7, 82.5 | Short of 4 Chunks of Boar Meat? Kill boars on the way back west
T 86 | "Auntie" Bernice Stonefield
A 84 | "Auntie" Bernice Stonefield
T 84 | Billy Maclure, at the vineyards
A 87 | Billy Maclure: Goldtooth has the necklace
C 62 | The Fargodeep Mine has two entrances in the hillside between the farms. Go in by the lower one (the eastern one, nearer the Maclures) and walk a little way in until "Scout through the Fargodeep Mine" ticks
C 87 | Goldtooth (level 8) stands in a side chamber of the lower tunnel (41.7, 78.0). Clear the Kobold Tunnelers near him, eat and drink to full, Imp out: Immolate from maximum range, Corruption, then Shadow Bolt until he is down. Loot Bernice's Necklace
C 47,60 | Kobold Tunnelers (5-6) and Miners (6-7) in the mine: collect 10 Gold Dust and 8 Large Candles. Miners stand deeper in and hit harder: one at a time
C 91775 @ Elwynn Forest, 39.0, 81.4 | 6 Lost Books lie on the ground and on crates through the mine; "Fun with Elementals" is in the deepest part, guarded (its spot is not published; the page warns the depths are dangerous). Clear slowly, one pull at a time, and drink to full before the last room. If the guard there is too much, leave the mine and press Skip on this step and its hand-in
T 87 | "Auntie" Bernice Stonefield, at the Stonefield Farm (the upper mine entrance comes out just above it)
H Goldshire | Hearthstone to the inn. On cooldown? Walk the road north, five minutes

